# printing.list — CUPS, as the Void handbook sets it up. A printer that
# works with AirPrint (IPP Everywhere) needs no driver at all; the
# drivers here cover older ones. HP's own hplip is left out (it
# is large, and newer HPs work without it): `xi hplip` adds it.
cups
cups-filters          # turns documents into what printers take
cups-pk-helper        # lets system-config-printer change printers without root
system-config-printer # add and manage printers (s-m → Printers)
avahi                 # finds printers on the network (avahi-daemon)
nss-mdns              # resolves their printer.local names; Void's nsswitch.conf already asks mdns
ipp-usb               # a driverless USB printer works like a network one
gutenprint            # drivers for many older inkjets
foomatic-db           # printer descriptions for older models
foomatic-db-engine
brother-brlaser       # Brother mono lasers
